## Notes

* `truncated_value` is the last `min(4, floor(length / 2))` characters of the
  value, with **no** mask prefix — measured across values of length 1 to 12, since
  the published API spec documents neither the field's shape nor its length. A
  12-character value gives up 4 characters, a 4-character value gives up 2, and a
  1-character value gives up none. This is a different shape from
  `circleci_project_environment_variables`' `value`, which prefixes the same kind
  of tail with `xxxx` — the two look alike and are not.
* Do not use `truncated_value` to detect that a value changed. Rotating a secret
  while keeping its last characters leaves it identical, so comparing it silently
  misses that class of rotation — a community CircleCI provider compares the mask
  and has exactly that gap. Compare `updated_at` instead.
* `updated_at` bumps on every write, including one that stores a byte-identical
  value, so it means "last written", not "last changed".
* `environment_variables` is always a list, empty when the context has none, so
  configurations can iterate over it unconditionally.
* The API returns the variables sorted by name. That ordering is what decides
  which variables fall inside the 100 the API discloses when a context holds more.
